{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols021BidirectionalDirectedA0P","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":" == "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Algorithms use this refinement to number the live vertices and edges with arrays while holes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exist, instead of hashing every vertex and edge they meet. The bounds are upper bounds only:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions are never reused, so a bound counts every position ever handed out, and nothing in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the library allocates by it. Position-keyed state goes through a paged map","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"_PositionNumbers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), O(live elements + pages).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Laws.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" In addition to ","type":"text"},{"code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"containsVertex(atPosition: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is true exactly for the positions of live vertices, all in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"0..<vertexPositionBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"vertexPosition(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"vertex(atPosition:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are inverse; and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the live vertices in increasing position. Likewise "},{"code":"containsEdge(atPosition:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for the positions in "},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", all in "},{"code":"0..<edgePositionBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", in increasing order."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Without holes, the bounds equal ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndexBound"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndexBound"},{"text":", and positions are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indices.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_numberedRows(outward:edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" numbers the live vertices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","te